Repair the program below and return a complete `solution.py`. Preserve its top-level API `select_context(records, query, limit)`.

`records` must be a list of dictionaries containing a unique non-empty string `id`, string `text`, and dictionary `metadata`. `query` must be a string. `limit` must be a non-negative integer, excluding booleans. Validate all records even when the query is empty or the limit is zero. Raise `ValueError` for malformed input.

Tokenization splits on whitespace and compares tokens case-insensitively. A record's score is the number of distinct query tokens appearing as exact tokens in its text. Exclude zero-score records. Sort by descending score and then ascending record ID. Return at most `limit` deep-copied records, each augmented with `score`. Empty queries, whitespace-only queries, zero limits, or no matches return an empty list. Do not mutate the input or retain mutable aliases to it.

